! colspan="3" |'''The Dual Era (1730–1960)'''
|-
|
|
|
* The war continued for several hundred years. During this time, '''giants''' and '''dragons''' were the dominant race.<ref name="C1067" />
*When a new balance between the five races was formed, the world had recovered some level of peace.<ref name="C1066" />
**The giants, elves, dragons, devils, and phoenixes coexisted, splitting up their rule over lands and seas.
**Vampires, demonic wolves, treants, sea monsters, mutants, and humans were vassals of the different factions, occupying the lower-middle classes.
|-
|
|{{tl-abbr|?}}
|
*The new generation of supernatural races gradually gained some level of rationality.<ref name="C1067" />
**[[Groselle]] and [[Siatas]] were born.
|-
|
|{{Tl-abbr|?}}
|
*The Ancient Gods had attempted to resolve the pollution of the [[Chaos Sea]] completely. Later, "They" gave up on the idea of directly exerting influence, and "They" switched focus to sealing and guarding it.<ref>{{Cite Book|1|1105}}</ref>
**[[Dragon of Imagination Ankewelt]] sealed the pollution of the [[Chaos Sea]] in [[Groselle's Travels]], and "He" hid the City of Miracle [[Liveseyd]] inside the subconsciousness of the book.<ref>{{Cite Book|1|1070}}</ref>
|-
